│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the dense per-qubit RY/RZ stack with a more parameter-efficient,       │
│                          │ symmetry-breaking hardware-efficient block.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Cut the per-block parameter count from 24 to 12 by sharing angles across structured     │
│                          │ qubit pairs.                                                                              │
│                          │ - Use three different pairing patterns across RX, RY, and RZ layers to avoid overly rigid │
│                          │ symmetry.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Add a fuller CZ entangling pattern: a ring plus long-range cross links, which better    │
│                          │ spreads feature-map correlations across the 8-qubit register.                             │
│                          │ - Keep only supported gates and preserve the fixed training loop, while improving         │
│                          │ generalization and parameter efficiency.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help reduce overfitting, lower gate count/depth, and improve the combined     │
│                          │ score without changing the fixed data pipeline.                                           │
