│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhance_entanglement_with_diagonal_crx                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a simple linear chain of CZ gates (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7). While this   │
│                          │ provides good basic entanglement, the topology limits information flow to nearest         │
│                          │ neighbors.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Keep the original RY layer (single-qubit rotations for flexibility)                    │
│                          │ 2. Keep initial RZ layer (state preparation)                                              │
│                          │ 3. Replace the linear CZ chain with a richer pattern:                                     │
│                          │    - First: Two-qubit ladder on even pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) with CZ                   │
│                          │    - Then: Offset pairs (1-2, 3-4, 5-6) with CZ to enable nearest-neighbor coupling       │
│                          │    - Finally: Add 4 parameterized CRX gates on diagonal pairs (0-2, 2-4, 4-6, 1-3) for    │
│                          │ adaptive entanglement learning                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Keep final RZ layer                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This topology improves expressivity by allowing the optimizer to learn both fixed and     │
│                          │ adaptive entanglement patterns. The diagonal parameterized gates target information flow  │
│                          │ across larger distances, which may help classify those remaining 2% of difficult cases.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected impact:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Modest parameter increase (4 more CRX params → 150 total)                               │
│                          │ - Better connectivity for information propagation                                         │
│                          │ - Potential improvement on edge cases while preserving good generalization                │
