│ patch_name               │ add_parametric_entangling_gates                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent results (combined_score 1.25) with perfect         │
│                          │ training accuracy, 0.99 validation accuracy, and fast convergence. However, it uses 146   │
│                          │ parameters with significant individual parameter allocation.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior programs shows:                                                         │
│                          │ - Program 2 (1.06 score, 74 params) used parametric two-qubit gates (CRZ) with smart      │
│                          │ parameter sharing for efficient entanglement                                              │
│                          │ - Current program (1.25 score, 146 params) uses only single-qubit rotations and fixed     │
│                          │ two-qubit gates                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To further improve while managing parameter efficiency, I propose:                        │
│                          │ 1. Keep the high-performing structure of individual RY and per-qubit RZ gates             │
│                          │ 2. Add parametric CRZ gates on diagonal qubit pairs with SHARED parameters (like program  │
│                          │ 2)                                                                                        │
│                          │ 3. Replace individual RZ post-CZ gates with parameter sharing (4 groups instead of 8      │
│                          │ individual)                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. This creates better expressiveness through controlled rotation entanglement while      │
│                          │ reducing total parameters from 146 to ~110 per block                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The parametric CRZ gates on diagonal pairs (0-4, 1-5, 2-6, 3-7) will enable the circuit   │
│                          │ to learn non-trivial correlations beyond fixed linear entanglement, following the proven  │
│                          │ strategy from program 2 but integrated with current's strong foundation.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome: Maintain or improve validation accuracy while reducing parameters and   │
│                          │ potentially improving parameter efficiency and generalization gap.                        │
