├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ long_distance_entanglement_sharing                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This proposal aims to improve the convergence speed and maintain high accuracy by         │
│                          │ introducing long-distance entanglement and parameter sharing within the ansatz block.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program uses a ring of CRY gates which provides nearest-neighbor              │
│                          │ connectivity. While effective, it can lead to slower information propagation across the   │
│                          │ 8-qubit register.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My modification:                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. Retains the initial RY rotation layer on all qubits for local expressivity.            │
│                          │ 2. Introduces a fixed CNOT ring to establish baseline entanglement without increasing     │
│                          │ parameter count.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Adds long-distance CRY gates (connecting qubits 0-4, 1-5, 2-6, and 3-7) to facilitate  │
│                          │ faster global correlation development.                                                    │
│                          │ 4. Adds a final RZ layer with shared parameters between opposite qubits (e.g., qubit 0    │
│                          │ and 4 share a parameter) to maintain the 16-parameter-per-block budget while adding phase │
│                          │ flexibility.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure maintains the efficient 98-parameter total but should accelerate           │
│                          │ convergence due to the improved connectivity graph.                                       │
