│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_cz_cry_hybrid_ansatz                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This evolution proposes a more parameter-efficient and faster-converging ansatz by        │
│                          │ combining fixed two-qubit gates (CZ) with a reduced number of parametrized entanglers     │
│                          │ (CRY).                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The previous 1.49 score was achieved using 8 RY gates and a ring of 8 CRY gates, totaling │
│                          │ 16 parameters per block (98 total parameters). My proposed block uses:                    │
│                          │ 1. A full layer of independent RY rotations (8 parameters) to maintain high expressive    │
│                          │ power for basis transformation.                                                           │
│                          │ 2. A fixed CZ ring to provide rapid entanglement without increasing the parameter count,  │
│                          │ which is expected to speed up Adam convergence (drawing inspiration from Seed 1's faster  │
│                          │ convergence).                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. A set of 4 long-range CRY cross-links (0-4, 1-5, 2-6, 3-7) to facilitate global        │
│                          │ information flow across the 8-qubit register. These use 4 independent parameters.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Total parameters per block are reduced from 16 to 12. This decreases the total model      │
│                          │ parameters from 98 to 74, significantly improving the `parameter_efficiency` metric. The  │
│                          │ combination of fixed circular entanglement and parametrized global bridges is designed to │
│                          │ maintain 100% accuracy while lowering the final loss and improving training speed.        │
