│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ collapse_cry_opposite_pairs                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves perfect test accuracy (1.00) and maximal combined score      │
│                          │ (1.49) with a cyclic CRY entangler on all 8 qubits, using 8 independent parameters (cry_0 │
│                          │ through cry_7). However, the ring structure exhibits rotational symmetry: opposite edge   │
│                          │ pairs (e.g., [0,1] and [4,5], or [1,2] and [5,6]) play structurally analogous roles.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By collapsing symmetric CRY edges into shared parameters—specifically grouping            │
│                          │ opposite-edge pairs—we reduce the per-block parameter count from 16 to 12 (8 RY + 4 CRY   │
│                          │ instead of 8 RY + 8 CRY). This cuts the total parameter budget from 98 to 74 while        │
│                          │ preserving the cyclic ring topology and the expressivity benefits of parameter tying      │
│                          │ across symmetric edges.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit tests the hypothesis that parameter sharing at symmetric positions maintains    │
│                          │ perfect accuracy at lower computational cost, potentially improving convergence speed     │
│                          │ (the current program takes 450 steps vs. 180 in a denser architecture) and parameter      │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
