│ patch_name               │ cry_ring_efficient_crossover                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from the prior programs. The key insight is     │
│                          │ that the second prior program achieves a superior combined score (1.49) with              │
│                          │ significantly better parameter efficiency (98 parameters vs 146 in the current program)   │
│                          │ and lower circuit depth (108 vs 99), using a simpler and more elegant ansatz structure.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second program's ansatz uses a ring of parametrized CRY gates connecting all qubits   │
│                          │ in a cycle (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7-0) preceded by independent RY rotations on each qubit. This   │
│                          │ creates a more compact and efficient entangling pattern compared to the current program's │
│                          │ approach of separate RZ pre/post rotations with fixed CZ gates.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By adopting the CRY ring structure from the second program while maintaining the robust   │
│                          │ training infrastructure, we expect to:                                                    │
│                          │ 1. Achieve perfect test accuracy (1.00 vs 0.98)                                           │
│                          │ 2. Reduce validation loss (0.04 vs 0.12)                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Improve parameter efficiency (0.01 vs lower)                                           │
│                          │ 4. Reduce generalization gap (0.00 vs 0.01)                                               │
│                          │ 5. Use fewer parameters overall while maintaining/exceeding performance                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a direct application of Occam's Razor in quantum circuit design: the simpler      │
│                          │ circuit with fewer, well-placed two-qubit gates outperforms the more complex structure.   │
