│ patch_description        │ This redesigned program shifts from a shallow, frequent re-uploading pattern              │
│                          │ (N_UPLOADS=3, N_REPEATS=2) to a deeper, less frequent one (N_UPLOADS=2, N_REPEATS=3).     │
│                          │ This structural change alters the feature-ansatz interleaving cadence:                    │
│                          │ - Prior: 3 feature uploads, each followed by 2 ansatz blocks                              │
│                          │ - New: 2 feature uploads, each followed by 3 ansatz blocks                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This consolidation may allow the ansatz blocks to work more coherently before the next    │
│                          │ feature re-encoding, potentially improving feature extraction and reducing the need for   │
│                          │ overfitting complexity. The ANSATZ_SPEC is simplified to a proven efficient design (RY    │
│                          │ rotations + CRY circular entanglement) with ~16 parameters per block, matching the best   │
│                          │ prior program's architecture. This reduces total circuit depth and gate count while       │
│                          │ maintaining expressivity, improving both convergence speed and generalization. The        │
│                          │ combined effect targets faster convergence (210→180 steps), better accuracy (0.99→1.00),  │
│                          │ lower loss (0.08→0.04), and better parameter efficiency.                                  │
